# Docker build context filter.
# Purpose: keep secrets, databases and build output OUT of the context that
# Docker sends to the daemon (they were traversing on every build: 1.6GB from
# .git + mobile/ + node_modules alone), and make accidental future COPYs of
# secrets impossible.
#
# Do NOT ignore anything the image needs:
#   - go.mod / go.sum                  (COPY at line 15)
#   - cmd/, internal/, db/             (go build ./cmd/server; db/migrations* are go:embed)
#   - internal/templates, internal/static, db/migrations (runtime COPY)
#   - .env.example                     (runtime COPY; negated below)

# VCS + tooling
.git
.github
.agents
.claude
.commandcode
.opencode
.zcode
.mcp.json
.cce

# Secrets / local config — never in the image
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
config/firebase-service-account.json
mobile/android/app/google-services.json

# Databases + runtime artifacts
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.db-journal
backups/
uploads/
*.log
server
server_*
bin/
audit-results.txt
playwright-report/
test-results/
strix_runs/

# Not needed to compile or run the server binary
node_modules
mobile
src
static
test
docs
scripts
hooks
coverage
*.out
openapi.yaml
ALL_TECH_SPECS.txt
